WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.247 --> 00:00:01.763
(energetic music)

00:00:01.763 --> 00:00:03.448
- [Voiceover] When I'm juggling,

00:00:03.448 --> 00:00:06.115
I feel like I have a superpower.

00:00:08.867 --> 00:00:11.171
To me it's just an amazing feeling

00:00:11.171 --> 00:00:12.647
to keep lots of things in the air

00:00:12.647 --> 00:00:15.730
and to keep these big patterns going.

00:00:21.266 --> 00:00:25.659
- [Voiceover] Sam Malcolm
is a combat juggler.

00:00:25.659 --> 00:00:29.767
The object of the sport is to
keep all three pins in the air

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:33.242
while preventing your
opponent from doing likewise.

00:00:33.242 --> 00:00:36.981
Light bumping and arm-to-arm
altercations are permitted.

00:00:36.981 --> 00:00:39.564
The last juggler standing wins.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.927
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.927 --> 00:00:47.031
- I got into combat juggling at about 3am

00:00:47.031 --> 00:00:49.114
at a juggling convention,

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:52.353
playing around with some friends,

00:00:52.353 --> 00:00:56.578
just trying to see who could
be the last one standing.

00:00:56.578 --> 00:00:57.996
We've all been to circuses.

00:00:57.996 --> 00:01:00.183
We've all seen variety acts.

00:01:00.183 --> 00:01:04.364
But this is something that
makes it more of a sport.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.335
If you're playing football,

00:01:05.335 --> 00:01:08.098
you have to put in the work
to get good at football.

00:01:08.098 --> 00:01:09.034
Juggling is no different.

00:01:09.034 --> 00:01:12.597
You have to put in hours and
hours and hours of practice.

00:01:12.597 --> 00:01:14.999
You're not only accounting
for the three objects

00:01:14.999 --> 00:01:16.172
that you're juggling,

00:01:16.172 --> 00:01:18.732
you have to anticipate that
there could be something flying

00:01:18.732 --> 00:01:21.943
at your head from 50 feet in the air,

00:01:21.943 --> 00:01:23.607
because it's so wild and crazy.

00:01:23.607 --> 00:01:25.175
There's so many other people playing.

00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:27.289
(audience exclaims)

00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:30.649
(upbeat music)

00:01:30.649 --> 00:01:32.281
I warm up for combat juggling.

00:01:32.281 --> 00:01:34.766
I jump rope for about 10 minutes.

00:01:34.766 --> 00:01:38.933
I work on balancing things
with my head and on my face.

00:01:40.036 --> 00:01:41.273
There's a lot of wild throws.

00:01:41.273 --> 00:01:42.612
There's a lot of wild saves.

00:01:42.612 --> 00:01:44.467
There's a lot of jumping
around and falling

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:45.710
and running on the ground,

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:49.725
and I try to go through all
of those things to get ready.

00:01:49.725 --> 00:01:51.677
You see incredible plays

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:54.300
by people like Steph
Curry or LeBron James.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.805
I can look at those people and tell you

00:01:55.805 --> 00:01:56.893
like they'd be great jugglers,

00:01:56.893 --> 00:02:00.755
'cause they have that awareness
over (laughs) their body.

00:02:00.755 --> 00:02:02.717
It's something new and exciting and fresh.

00:02:02.717 --> 00:02:03.944
It's something fun.

00:02:03.944 --> 00:02:04.817
It's something different.

00:02:04.817 --> 00:02:06.371
(audience exclaims)

00:02:06.371 --> 00:02:08.449
So I'm optimistic that it'll grow

00:02:08.449 --> 00:02:10.204
and become something really great.

00:02:10.204 --> 00:02:12.787
(upbeat music)

